  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * @defgroup Conv Convolution
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Convolution is a mathematical operation that operates on two finite length vectors to generate a
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Convolution is similar to correlation and is frequently used in filtering and data analysis.
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * The CMSIS DSP library contains functions for convolving Q7, Q15, Q31, and floating-point data ty
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * The library also provides fast versions of the Q15 and Q31 functions on Cortex-M4 and Cortex-M3.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par Algorithm
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Let <code>a[n]</code> and <code>b[n]</code> be sequences of length <code>srcALen</code> and <cod
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Then the convolution
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *                   c[n] = a[n] * b[n]
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * is defined as
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \image html ConvolutionEquation.gif
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Note that <code>c[n]</code> is of length <code>srcALen + srcBLen - 1</code> and is defined over 
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * <code>pSrcA</code> points to the first input vector of length <code>srcALen</code> and
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * <code>pSrcB</code> points to the second input vector of length <code>srcBLen</code>.
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * The output result is written to <code>pDst</code> and the calling function must allocate <code>s
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Conceptually, when two signals <code>a[n]</code> and <code>b[n]</code> are convolved,
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * the signal <code>b[n]</code> slides over <code>a[n]</code>.
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * For each offset \c n, the overlapping portions of a[n] and b[n] are multiplied and summed togeth
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Note that convolution is a commutative operation:
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *                   a[n] * b[n] = b[n] * a[n].
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * This means that switching the A and B arguments to the convolution functions has no effect.
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * <b>Fixed-Point Behavior</b>
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Convolution requires summing up a large number of intermediate products.
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * As such, the Q7, Q15, and Q31 functions run a risk of overflow and saturation.
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Refer to the function specific documentation below for further details of the particular algorit
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * <b>Fast Versions</b>
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Fast versions are supported for Q31 and Q15.  Cycles for Fast versions are less compared to Q31 
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccVpnDhb.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * the input signals should be scaled down to avoid intermediate overflows.
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * <b>Opt Versions</b>
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  *
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * \par
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * Opt versions are supported for Q15 and Q7.  Design uses internal scratch buffer for getting good
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  * These versions are optimised in cycles and consumes more memory(Scratch memory) compared to Q15 
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_f32.c ****  */
